  "question": {
    "text": "The intercept on the line $y=x$ by the circle $x^2+y^2-2 x=0$ is $A B$. Equation of the circle on $\\mathrm{AB}$ as a diameter is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2-x-y=0$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2-x+y=0$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{x}^2+\\mathrm{y}^2+\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y}=0$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$x^2+y^2+x-y=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Points of intersection of line $y=x$ with $x^2+y^2-2 x=0$ are $(0,0)$ and $(1,1)$ hence equation of circle having end points of diameter $(0,0)$ and $(1,1)$ is $x^2+y^2-x-y=0$"
  }
}